    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0311" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg215"/>

                <head>No. 176.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Sir Edward
                    Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 30,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to state that this
                    Department is informed by a letter of 29th instant, from the Acting Secretary of
                    the Navy, that instructions have been sent to Commander Byron Wilson, commanding
                    the United States steamer Yantic, to co-operate with Sir II. B. E. Frere, the
                    agent of Her Britannic Majesty’s government, in any proper way to secure the
                    success of his mission to Muscat or Zanzibar.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
